@startwbs
' GUI element-detection problem-space taxonomy (from UIED, Xie et al. 2020).
' WBS layout is pure-Java (no Graphviz/Smetana needed). Keep ASCII-only.
<style>
wbsDiagram {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  LineColor #666666
  node {
    Padding 8
    Margin 6
    FontName Arial
    FontSize 12
    RoundCorner 8
  }
  arrow { LineColor #888888 }
}
</style>

* GUI element detection\nproblem space
** <back:#FFF3E0>Element level</back>
*** <back:#FFE0B2>Large intra-class variation\n(one class, many sizes/shapes/styles)
*** <back:#FFE0B2>High inter-class similarity\n(button vs spinner: subtle cues)
** <back:#E3F2FD>GUI level
*** <back:#BBDEFB>Heterogeneous mix\n(widgets + images + text)
*** <back:#BBDEFB>Dense / adjacent elements\n(packed, few-pixel gaps)
*** <back:#BBDEFB>High-precision region\n(a loose box is not enough)
@endwbs
